// The Veteran cape, for the players who tested the server before it opened.
//
// THE MESH IS THE ATTACK CAPE'S, MENDED, and it is written by tools/models/genveterancape.py.
// Rerun that rather than editing the .ob2 files. tools/models/genveterancapemesh.py built a cape
// from scratch for three rounds and is superseded; it is kept only for what it recorded.
//
// WHAT HAD TO BE MENDED. The attack cape has a hole in the middle of its back - strip its emblem,
// render it with nothing behind, and the background shows through. Jagex's solid emblem covers
// that gap rather than closing it. Our device is the rank's own chat icon, an open shape, so it
// needed a disc behind it to cover the same gap, and that disc was the only reason the cape ever
// had a circle on it. Building a whole cape to avoid the disc was the wrong answer: eight faces
// fanned from the hole's own boundary close it, and keeping Jagex's mesh keeps the drape, the
// fold, the collar, the animation labels and the draw priorities that a hand-built sheet kept
// getting wrong.
//
// THE DEVICE SITS AT THE DEPTH OF THE EMBLEM IT REPLACED, not at the front of the cape. Taking
// the cape's frontmost cloth instead put it at depth 20-26 against cloth at 14-20, and in game it
// floated off the back. See genveterancape.py, which says so where the number is worked out.
//
// A MAX CAPE VARIANT IS MADE FROM THIS ONE. Use it on a Max cape with a Max hood and all three
// become a Veteran max cape and its hood - scripts/skillcapes, generated from
// tools/maxcapevariantspec.json. That cape is NOT this mesh: it is the Max cape's own model with
// its red cloth recoloured to this bronze and this device struck into the back, written by
// tools/genveteranmaxcape.py. The device is placed differently there - its vertices take their
// animation labels from the cloth under each one rather than sharing a single label, because the
// Max cape's back is a patchwork of five of them where the attack cape's emblem sits on one.
//
// The engine knows about the variant: World.veteranCape counts a fused cape as still having one,
// or it would hand out a free Veteran cape at every login, and taking the rank away splits the
// variant rather than destroying a Max cape somebody earned with twenty-three ninety-nines.
//
// The bronze is the same ramp the Veteran chat icon is drawn in, so the rank reads as one thing
// in chat and on the back, and the device is the chat icon's own shape. It is dark against the
// cloth, which is this shape's idiom - a skillcape wears a dark grey sword on a gold shield.
//
// NO RECOLOURS HERE, unlike every other cape in the build: the colours are generated into the
// models. A shared mesh recoloured per item needs a list of colour pairs, and a list is a thing
// that can fall out of step with a mesh.
//
// THE DEFENCE IS A PLAIN CAPE'S, deliberately. This is a badge: a reward that is also an upgrade
// would pull against the launch wipe, which exists to put everyone on the same footing. A Cape of
// Accomplishment's +9 would have made it worth wearing for its stats.
//
// Untradeable, and given back by the server to any veteran who does not have one - see
// Engine-TS World.grantVeteranCape. Losing it costs nothing but a relog.

[veteran_cape]
name=Veteran cape
desc=Worn by those who tested Death Plateau before it opened.
model=obj_veteran_cape
manwear=obj_veteran_cape_manwear,0
womanwear=obj_veteran_cape_womanwear,0
// The Attack cape's own camera. It suits a cape LYING DOWN, which is what the inventory model
// is again: looking straight at a standing cape, as an earlier version did, gave a readable icon
// and an unreadable lump on the ground, because the ground uses this same model.
2dzoom=2128
2dxan=504
2dyof=1
iop2=Wear
wearpos=back
cost=1
tradeable=no
weight=1lb
category=armour_cape
param=slashdefence,1
param=crushdefence,1
param=rangedefence,2
